>>hack.c:822:                 pline("Trapping your pet was a selfish move.");
>>objnam.c:912:        (!strcmp(spot-3, "fish") || !strcmp(spot-3, "tuna") ||
>>-- 
>Fish? Tuna? I don't recognize these either...
>(And here I thought I knew a lot about NH :) )

This one took me by surprise.  This seems to be in some section where
they figure out plurals of names for fruit.  Fish and tuna (among several
others) are already plural.  I really can't believe they bothered to code
the plural if you name your favorite fruit "fish".  TUTTI_FRUTTI has to
be the most intricate totally useless feature in nethack.

Granted, it does produce the funniest message in the game (when you 
rename your favorite fruit 100 times to 100 different things), but
this checking for plurals boggles my mind.  Reading the comments, it
looks like the dev team was almost embarrased that it doesn't work
properly for swine, trout, and grouse.
